# Files that must not ship to the sutton Vercel project.
#
# Vercel serves the Root Directory as a static filesystem, so anything
# uploaded here is publicly fetchable. The ee2fa18 deployment listed 17 static
# assets: SPEC.md, 11 .py files, requirements.txt, three test files and the
# 8000-line history fixture were all reachable by URL.
#
# Two layers fix that, most-sensitive-first:
#   1. This file removes what the function never imports, so it is not
#      uploaded at all.
#   2. vercel.json sets outputDirectory to public/, so the static root holds
#      only that directory and the remaining runtime modules are not served.
#
# Only remove something here if api/index.py genuinely does not import it,
# directly or transitively. As of this commit the function needs exactly:
#   checks.py interpret.py packet.py redact.py render.py store.py validate.py
# plus requirements.txt.

SPEC.md
tests/
build_fixture.py
diagnose.py
radar.py
replay.py
smoke.sh
